  "title": "Faxian's pilgrimage to India",
  "summary": "In 399 the Buddhist monk Faxian left Chang'an on foot and travelled by Dunhuang, Khotan and the Pamirs into India, visiting Buddhist sites. He stayed at Pataliputra from 405 to 407, then at Tamralipti, and spent about two years in Sri Lanka, collecting texts. After storms and a stop in Sumatra, his ship landed on the Shandong peninsula in 412.",
